WEBVTT

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:49.640
Okay, five seconds. Four, three, two...

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:52.860
Let's broadcast live again today!

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:54.090
Ready, go!

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.290
Full-Throttle Gil-Gil Night!

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:56.760
"Oh, My! Gil-Gil Swimming
Contest Full of Women"

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:57.760
Yay!

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:58.160
"Oh, My! Gil-Gil Swimming
Contest Full of Women"

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:00.590
"Full-Throttle Gil-Gil Night"

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:04.470
Howdy there! I'm your emcee, "Bottled Beer Ohnogi"!

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:07.040
And I'm his assistant, Kyoko Iwashima!

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:11.840
Hey, Kyoko, the atmosphere seems
a little different than usual tonight!

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:13.780
That's right! Today on "Gil-Night,"

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:17.450
we're here at our specially-made
studio set at the Urayasu City Pool,

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:22.720
bringing you the off-season special
"Gil-Gil Swimming Contest Full of Women"!

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:23.120
- What's with this program?

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.490
- What's with this program?
- Let's really get the audience fired up, everybody!

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:28.190
- There's no help for it, nosiree.
Ms. Irma gave us this job, Sir.
- Let's really get the audience fired up, everybody!

00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:30.160
Yay!

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:33.630
Even so... this is no way to dress!

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:36.470
Really? I think it's cute, yessiree.

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:37.070
- You have a complaint about how I look, Sir?

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:38.370
- Okay, let's begin by introducing
our special guest, Shion Arita!

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:42.300
- No, that's not what I mean...

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:46.080
Ah, right! I'm Shion Arita, yessiree!

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:49.080
I'll give it my all, as always!

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:50.070
Tee-hee!

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:55.810
Oh, no! You shouldn't do that!

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:58.550
Did you see it, Hazawa?!

00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:01.260
I saw it! Shion is just so cute!

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:04.760
Of course she is! She's our Akiba idol!

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:08.000
She's in a different class
than those small-fry nobodies!

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.200
They were watching that?

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.870
Sorry, I know you just pulled an all-nighter,

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:15.240
but we have to get to that place Irma told us about.

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:16.710
Oh, I guess so.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:17.610
What?

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:22.850
Ah, nothing. I'm going to head out.

00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:24.010
Oh.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:28.180
What about you? Is your
Journalism Club investigation going okay?

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:30.350
Well, so-so.

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:32.950
Muroto's not reliable help...

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:37.190
Your shop never changes.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:41.360
It's as dingy as ever,
and you only have unpopular books.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:43.030
You never change either.

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:44.130
Really?

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:47.570
Yep. You're the same as you
were in your student days.

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:51.470
Sheesh. I guess someone as old
as you will still treat me like a kid, huh?

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:54.310
"Mille Plateaux"

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:56.880
This is a good book, eh?

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:57.870
Yeah.

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:10.220
"Tamaki Pub"

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:16.300
Sorry, honey, we're not open yet.

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:21.500
I don't drink alcohol. I just
want to talk to you, Tamaki Saito...

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:24.070
...no, Kuruksu.

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:27.910
Wh-Who are you?!

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:32.150
I'm a Federation investigator.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:36.290
I'd like to ask you some questions
about illicit mimesis chip sales.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:38.520
Wh-Whatever are you talking about?

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:40.620
Don't play dumb!

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:42.610
Wh-What are you doing?!

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:49.670
Huh?

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:51.870
You sold mimesis chips recently, didn't you?

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:53.800
I-I don't know anything!

00:04:53.800 --> 00:05:01.140
And even if I did, I wouldn't
say a thing without a lawyer...

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:04.310
Sorry, but I haven't got the time. Hurry up and talk!

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:06.820
I-I've sold six of them recently.

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:07.810
To who?

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:13.690
Yeah, I remember that.

00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:17.890
Whoops, sorry, I'm supposed to meet someone.

00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:19.500
I'll come back another time!

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:23.070
Okay, see you later.

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:27.840
What did that boy come for, anyway?

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:29.240
Dusk.

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:37.750
Do you remember me?

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:42.480
Yes. You're Birdy.

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:43.880
Come with me.

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:55.090
What is it, Dad?

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:03.240
B-Birdy!

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:06.230
You said you had no contact with your dad.

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:09.950
I'm sorry.

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:13.920
I didn't want you to see him the way he is now.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:16.750
You helped the escapees, didn't you?

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:19.190
Please tell me.

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:21.590
You see, Birdy...

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:30.970
I was once a member of
the Altan liberation front... the Isdalta.

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:32.470
Dad!

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:37.640
Yes, I know what it means to mention that name.

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:40.440
They claim to stand for
Altan liberation and Altan rights,

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:43.880
but they're a terrorist group.

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:48.620
And they were behind the Central Tower Incident.

00:06:48.620 --> 00:06:51.920
You don't understand...

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:56.960
You don't understand anything!

00:06:56.960 --> 00:06:58.390
P-Please wait!

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:01.230
Dad didn't have anything to do with that bombing.

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:03.630
He cut ties to the group before that!

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:05.070
That day...

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:09.940
Dusk, you really mean to drop out?

00:07:09.940 --> 00:07:12.740
Do you know what the higher-ups are trying to do?!

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:15.780
They're trying to join forces with Christella Revi!

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:18.410
Wow, now ain't that grand?

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:23.090
Revi climbed to the top of the
Ministry of Science despite being an Altan.

00:07:23.090 --> 00:07:26.080
For someone like that to
about-face and go to bat for us...

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:34.920
Fine, I get it. You're a coward
who's started to fear for his life!

00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:43.310
Dad...

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:46.300
This is something you mustn't get involved in.

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:52.540
And then the Central Tower was bombed.

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:02.660
You know what kind of
persecution Altans faced after that.

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:05.830
Dad and I narrowly managed to
escape Oriotera with our lives,

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:08.460
and we came to Earth.

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:13.300
But... then <i>he</i> showed up again.

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:17.810
It's no big deal, I just need
you to coach them a little.

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:20.080
Come on, for old times' sake.

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:24.910
I refuse. I have no intention
of cooperating with you people.

00:08:24.910 --> 00:08:27.320
You sure you're not
misunderstanding something here?

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:32.150
I don't care about your
"cooperation." This is a <i>threat.</i>

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:34.690
Do you think I'd just quietly let them catch me?

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:36.990
I'd bring you down with me.

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:41.060
And that reject brat too, while I'm at it.

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:46.340
Please believe me. Dad did it for me...

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:48.540
Just tell me one thing.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:52.710
Valic was involved in the bombing too, wasn't he?

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:55.580
Yes.

00:08:55.580 --> 00:08:57.570
Where are the escapees?

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:04.590
This is their info. Do what you like with it.

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:06.020
Tuto.

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:16.120
So this is where Valic is hiding out.

00:09:27.410 --> 00:09:30.410
Hey! Please, explain this to me, Birdy!

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:33.320
What the heck is "Isdalta"? Birdy!

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:34.300
Birdy!

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:41.290
Colonel, it's the investigator.

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:46.400
I knew it. Don't hurt that man;
we owe him a little something.

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:48.930
I'll have to invite him out <i>personally.</i>

00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:49.920
Yes, Sir.

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:55.500
What do you mean to do?

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:56.470
Nataru!

00:09:56.470 --> 00:10:00.810
Don't you get it, Dad? Birdy let us slide!

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:04.310
But she's a Federation investigator,
so she's sure to file a report.

00:10:04.310 --> 00:10:06.140
We have to get away while we can.

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:17.120
Let's go, Dad!

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:29.300
Moss, eh?

00:10:29.300 --> 00:10:32.710
Huh? The Federation investigator?

00:10:32.710 --> 00:10:35.880
So she's made contact with Dusk.

00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:38.150
You want us to run?

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:39.140
Understood.

00:10:42.520 --> 00:10:44.120
It's too bad.

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:47.860
I liked this life, too...

00:10:47.860 --> 00:10:54.820
Ribbit.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:11.510
Damn that Valic! He got away?

00:11:11.510 --> 00:11:16.520
Birdy, there's something on the wall.

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:18.920
It says "moron"!

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:35.170
Stay here for a while, got it, Dad?

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:38.210
It wouldn't be so bad to get captured by her.

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:39.740
Give me a break!

00:11:39.740 --> 00:11:44.110
If you're going to say that now, then
you shouldn't have helped them escape!

00:11:44.110 --> 00:11:50.720
Plus, it'd be hard on Birdy.

00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:55.120
I'll find a new house right away,
so behave yourself until then.

00:12:17.410 --> 00:12:18.580
Is that the place?

00:12:18.580 --> 00:12:19.570
Yes, Sir.

00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:29.990
Room service, Sir.

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:31.960
Room service?

00:12:31.960 --> 00:12:32.950
Sir?

00:12:36.430 --> 00:12:40.670
You sure you don't have the wrong
room? I didn't order anything.

00:12:40.670 --> 00:12:44.140
I did.

00:12:44.140 --> 00:12:49.240
I ordered it for you.

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:50.640
Gatol...

00:12:56.150 --> 00:12:58.790
Your room service is here, Dusk.

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:02.320
I came to get you.

00:13:02.320 --> 00:13:04.530
Oh, we won't cause you any trouble.

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:07.430
We just have something we want to ask you.

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:10.420
How about you come with us?

00:13:37.230 --> 00:13:38.660
Dad!

00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:48.870
He doesn't seem to be armed.

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:54.080
Agrazume and Rianshel were murdered.
I trust you're aware of that?

00:13:54.080 --> 00:14:00.250
Yes. The cessation of their life
functions was recorded on the telemeter.

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:02.650
Why do you think they died?

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:05.150
Unfortunately, I don't know that.

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:07.690
Someone is targeting us.

00:14:07.690 --> 00:14:11.360
What's more, they seem to know who we really are.

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:12.730
Why would that be?

00:14:12.730 --> 00:14:16.000
I have no idea.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:20.340
You're the only possibility, Dusk! Who hired you?!

00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:22.440
What are you talking about?

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:24.910
I would never sell out a client.

00:14:24.910 --> 00:14:26.340
I wonder about that.

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:38.090
So that's the sleight of hand
you're known for, Blue Fang?

00:14:38.090 --> 00:14:39.080
Moss.

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:43.850
I see.

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:49.390
You were called the "Blue Fang," after all.

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:10.950
Nataru...

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:20.730
Hmph. So cheeky for an Altan.

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:21.600
Colonel?!

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:24.220
Calm yourself. It's just a scratch.

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:34.940
But for an Altan, being able to
injure me at all is quite impressive.

00:15:34.940 --> 00:15:38.780
So now there's no one targeting us anymore, right?

00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:40.150
Right.

00:15:40.150 --> 00:15:43.920
It's over now.

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:47.160
Valic, go dump the corpse outside.

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:48.140
Yeah, yeah.

00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:51.090
Hey, Birdy.

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:52.460
What?

00:15:52.460 --> 00:15:54.600
What's "Isdalta"?

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:57.930
The name of an antigovernment
group in the Federation.

00:15:57.930 --> 00:16:00.270
And the "Central Tower Incident"?

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:02.100
It's none of your business.

00:16:02.100 --> 00:16:08.940
Well, probably not, but... Birdy, you've been
acting strange ever since it was mentioned.

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:12.810
No, I haven't. I'm acting just like normal.

00:16:12.810 --> 00:16:14.210
Birdy...

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:41.510
Hello?

00:16:41.510 --> 00:16:43.580
Nataru! Nataru!

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:45.910
What is it, Kuruksu?

00:16:45.910 --> 00:16:49.050
It's an emergency, that's what it is!

00:16:49.050 --> 00:16:52.250
Dusk is... Your father is!

00:16:52.250 --> 00:16:53.240
What?

00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:12.540
"Shinmyou Books"

00:17:12.540 --> 00:17:14.540
I guess that was a premonition...
"Shinmyou Books"

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:15.440
"Shinmyou Books"

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:25.120
Shion Arita?

00:17:29.760 --> 00:17:31.760
It's finally quieted down.

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:35.760
Dad did run his business in Kanda for a long time...

00:17:35.760 --> 00:17:38.900
Oh, I'm sorry, I don't drink alcohol.

00:17:38.900 --> 00:17:42.400
Okay. I'll pour you a soft drink, then.

00:17:42.400 --> 00:17:43.740
Here.

00:17:43.740 --> 00:17:45.140
Thanks.

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:53.650
Say, do you remember this?

00:17:57.550 --> 00:18:00.390
A kilk. This brings back memories!

00:18:03.990 --> 00:18:07.800
Dad made them for me when we were little.

00:18:07.800 --> 00:18:14.100
I loved them, so we played
with them a lot when I visited you.

00:18:14.100 --> 00:18:19.100
I remember you squeezed one apart
right away, and really gave Dad a headache.

00:18:25.810 --> 00:18:27.250
Nataru...

00:18:29.680 --> 00:18:31.680
<i>I'm sorry, Birdy.</i>

00:18:46.670 --> 00:18:49.100
Are you Faroid?

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:51.110
Y-Yes.

00:18:51.110 --> 00:18:53.340
You're Dusk's?

00:18:53.340 --> 00:18:56.810
You needed two, right? Where's your sister?

00:18:56.810 --> 00:19:01.120
She's sleeping. Never mind that,
just give them to me.

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:03.650
I need a new face.

00:19:03.650 --> 00:19:07.020
First I have one question.

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:09.820
Are you the one who killed my dad?

00:19:09.820 --> 00:19:14.830
l-It wasn't me! It was Gatol
and the others who killed Dusk!

00:19:14.830 --> 00:19:17.700
Do you swear by the holy spawning finger?

00:19:17.700 --> 00:19:20.690
Yeah, I swear on the holy finger.

00:19:24.070 --> 00:19:25.900
Thanks for telling me.

00:19:37.720 --> 00:19:42.020
Wh-Why? l-I didn't do anything...

00:19:42.020 --> 00:19:46.090
Not true. You released the Ryunka.

00:19:46.090 --> 00:19:48.090
Why do you?

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:54.700
W-Wait! I only did research!

00:19:54.700 --> 00:19:59.700
The one who said we should use it was...

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:13.680
Don't...

00:20:21.130 --> 00:20:23.570
Sp-Spare me...

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:27.040
I'm sure the people who died
here wanted the same thing.

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:30.440
But they didn't even have
the time to form the words.

00:20:34.280 --> 00:20:39.270
These ruins are the most
fitting place for your graves!

00:20:44.320 --> 00:20:45.750
Dad...

00:21:00.500 --> 00:21:01.730
Faroid!

00:21:06.840 --> 00:21:10.830
He was my brother, born of the twelfth egg...

00:21:18.950 --> 00:21:21.960
H-Huh? Was I asleep?

00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:27.950
Yeah. But that let me talk to my Dad one-on-one.

00:21:30.030 --> 00:21:34.800
I promise you, I'll catch the murderer... I promise.

00:21:34.800 --> 00:21:36.870
Thank you...

00:21:36.870 --> 00:21:38.300
...Birdy.

00:23:12.030 --> 00:23:15.040
<i>This is Birdy Cephon Altira.</i>

00:23:15.040 --> 00:23:21.110
<i>Now even Faroid's been killed, and</i>
<i>the escapees seem to think I did it.</i>

00:23:21.110 --> 00:23:24.750
<i>So they lure me out...</i>

00:23:24.750 --> 00:23:30.620
<i>And then Tsutomu and I are in big trouble!</i>

00:23:30.620 --> 00:23:34.610
<i>Violin, what's going to happen to me?</i>
